// A dedicated signing key kept OUTSIDE this repo, at a stable path in the user's own
// profile (not any project or temp directory - both get wiped/regenerated by unrelated
// tooling on a dev machine, e.g. Android Studio/AVD Manager can recreate the *shared*
// ~/.android/debug.keystore that AGP falls back to by default). Every build signed with
// a different key forces Android to treat it as a different app: installing it can only
// replace the old one via a full uninstall, which wipes all alarms/settings instead of
// updating in place. Pinning one key here is what makes "install the new APK over the old
// one" behave like an actual update. If this file isn't present (e.g. building fresh on a
// different machine), the build quietly falls back to the platform's normal debug signing
// instead of failing - it just won't update cleanly over a build signed with this key.
val kuclabKeystore = file(System.getProperty("user.home") + "/.android/kuclab-clock.keystore")

